{title: I Bless Your Name}
{key: C}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]In prisoners' [C]chains [F]with bleeding [C]stripes[F][C]
[C]Paul and [Am]Silas [F]prayed that [G]night
And in their [C]pain be[F]gan to [C]sing[Am]
[Am]Their chains were [C]loosed and [F]they were [C]free[F][C]

{comment: Chorus 1}
[C]I bless Your name, [F]I bless Your [C]name
[C]I give You [Am]honor, [F]give You [G]praise
You are the [C]Life, [F]the Truth, the [C]Way
[Am]I bless Your [C]name, I [F]bless Your [C]name

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]Some midnight [C]hour [F]if you should [C]find[F][C]
[C]You're in a [Am]prison [F]in your [G]mind
Reach out and [C]praise, [F]defy [C]those [Am]chains
[Am]And they will [C]fall in Je[F]sus' [C]name[F][C]

{comment: Chorus 2}
[C]We bless Your name, [F]we bless Your [C]name
[C]We give You [Am]honor, [F]give You [G]praise
You are the [C]Life, [F]the Truth, the [C]Way
[Am]We bless Your [C]name, we [F]bless Your [C]name
